// Typecheck settings for EMITTED TypeScript (issue #198).
//
// `tsconfig.json` includes `golden/**` and nothing else, so the modules
// `scripts/emit-fixtures.ts` writes into `tests/generated/` — the ones the
// vitest suites actually import and execute — were never typechecked. For a
// compiler backend that is most of what the target language buys us: the
// emitter could produce type-incorrect TypeScript and stay green as long as
// the code happened to RUN. Widening the check found a real defect the day it
// first ran (`Frame.transactional`/`transactionalMethod` typed their inverse's
// parameter `unknown`, so every emitted `(result) => undo(result)` was a type
// error — 21 of them across five modules).
//
// This is a SEPARATE config, not a widened `include` on the main one, for two
// reasons.
//
// 1. Generated code legitimately wants looser STYLISTIC settings than
//    hand-written source. The emitter binds every crossing argument to a
//    `$revl_wit<N>_acq_argN` local whether or not the inverse reads it, so
//    `noUnusedLocals`/`noUnusedParameters` report 19 findings here, none of
//    them a defect. `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` reports 69, all on indexing the
//    emitter itself proved in-bounds. Every SEMANTIC check stays on: this
//    config inherits `strict` from the base and turns nothing off that could
//    hide a wrong type.
//
// 2. Emitted modules must be checked ONE PROGRAM PER MODULE, which a plain
//    `tsc -p` cannot express. Each `emit.py` invocation produces a standalone
//    program, and each one augments cordis' global `Context`
//    (`declare module 'cordis' { interface Context { db: Database } }`). Put
//    two modules that both provide a `db` in one program and TypeScript merges
//    the augmentations, reports TS2717, and then resolves `ctx.db` to the
//    WRONG interface — 7 spurious errors across the fixture set, none of which
//    says anything about the emitter. `scripts/typecheck-generated.mjs` reads
//    this file and builds a program per root; it is the entry point, not `tsc
//    -p tsconfig.generated.json`.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    // Stylistic, OFF — see (1). Listed explicitly rather than inherited-absent
    // so that turning one on in the base config does not silently start
    // reporting non-defects here.
    "noUnusedLocals": false,
    "noUnusedParameters": false
  },
  // `golden/**` is emitted output too — checked-in rather than regenerated per
  // run, but produced by the same emitter — and it belongs under the same
  // one-program-per-module rule (issue #223). It used to ride along in
  // tsconfig.json's group program, which worked only for as long as no two
  // golden fixtures provided the same service name.
  "include": ["tests/generated/**/*.ts", "golden/**/*.ts"]
}
